00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
now that we've had more time to look  over call of duty black ops cold war  multiplayer and listen to community  reactions  it's time to round up the biggest  differences between cold war and modern  warfare and say which one we feel might  have the advantage right now  let's start by talking about movement  there's already been a bit of  controversy around movement in cold war  after the multiplayer reveal  pro players who got their hands on the  game already lobbied for greater  penalties around slide cancelling which  can be abused to aim faster and sprint  longer than other players  there are also some huge questions still  in the air around which systems will go  into war zone  for example if it sticks with modern  warfare mechanics and not cold wars then  cold war players will have to develop  two completely different sets of muscle  memory going between modes  with that in mind let's dig a little bit  deeper into movement for starters cold  war  doesn't have the tactical sprint from  modern warfare where you're able to gain  a speed boost to cover large areas of  ground while holding your gun up in the  air  instead cold war has a system where you  always get an initial boost of speed  then quickly settle into normal run  speed  this should allow you to quickly duck  behind nearby cover like modern warfare  but you won't be able to cover those  large patches of ground  speaking of running into things there  doesn't seem to be doors in cold war  i'm not sure how much you realize you're  used to doors in modern warfare  doors are everywhere in modern warfare  and you use them for cover to set up  ambushes to listen for enemy players  entering buildings we're honestly gonna  miss not having them in cold war  and probably also going to slide into a  lot of unusable doors for a long time  next up swimming it's back and honestly  it's about  time it's been very strange avoiding the  water in modern warfare  just an all-around good addition in cold  war when it comes to jumping  cold war has what they're calling a  classic jump it seems to involve a fast  takeoff with a slowdown penalty on  landing to avoid abuse  modern warfare has a different system  where if you jump rapidly  the jumps get shorter and shorter and  shorter when it comes to maps though  modern warfare has these really clever  map routes with unexpected places to  jump and mantle to  so far we've only seen more controlled  routes like zip lines and fast rubs from  cold war  when it comes to the slide cold war has  a pretty fast slide that players could  abuse in the alpha and that's  already sort of being addressed as it  stands cold war does not appear to have  executions which are honestly pretty  rare to see in modern warfare  but so satisfying when you pull them off  it's something that we'll miss in core  multiplayer but we're assuming we'll  still be in the shared war zone mode  finally let's talk about feel we're not  exactly comparing apples to apples here  since cold war is an alpha and modern  warfare has been out for over a year now  but we can't shake the feeling that cold  war just  feels a little stiffer maybe even like a  step back in how players move and  interact with their environment  we'll just have to stay tuned on this  one all right so now let's talk about  gun play and loadouts  so far gun play and loadouts are a mixed  bag of improvements and  maybe setbacks to modern warfare  starting with feelings  the recoil in cold war seems to be more  in line with black ops 4 than modern  warfare  it leans towards less recoil and more  control that probably means you can more  easily use a wider range of weapons but  at the expense of individual guns having  that unique feel they do in modern  warfare  the created class system in cold war  does seem very similar to modern warfare  with slightly fewer gun attachments by  default  it also brings back the wild card system  which means you can bring your guns in  line with the number of attachments in  modern warfare or do some slightly more  creative builds  one place create a class is a big  improvement over modern warfare is in  how weapon attachments list specific  stat changes to guns  modern warfare relies on pretty vague  descriptions of what gun attachments do  and sometimes it's just outright  confusing for example how suppressors in  modern warfare do or don't interact with  the minimap  compass and uavs right now we're giving  a slight advantage here to cold war  so now you got your guns built you're  going along you're making kills let's  talk about  score streaks cold war will have a  scorestreak system that does not reset  when you die  whether you like that or not is a  personal preference some people do like  kill streaks but score streaks make low  end rewards more accessible for more  people  and also reward you for playing  objectives you'll still need to chain  together multiple kills and objective  captures to earn score streak bonuses  that get the higher end and more deadly  call-ins  there's also going to be counter-score  streaks which is kind of a plus  currently modern warfare relies on  players to manually shoot down  deadly kill streaks like chopper gunner  it's really a mixed bag  in some random matches people are really  good but in other ones they refuse to  deal with it and your team gets  murderized  kill streaks in modern warfare really  don't incentivize support playstyles  and we really like that cold war does  something else really cool with cold war  is it gives you the actual percentage of  your contribution when you capture  objectives  now if we could only find some way to  convince random players that you only  need to hold  two of three objectives in domination  when it comes to other aspects of your  loadout cold war seems to have a near  identical field upgrade support gadget  system to modern warfare  it's based on earning momentary  power-ups over time  cold war does bring back the sam turret  which will help the average player deal  with high-end score streaks better  by shooting down air assets honestly  when it comes to building your loadouts  and classes right now  cold war seems to have a slight  advantage alright so let's talk about  modes  how are you going to feel about cold  war's modes probably comes down to what  attracted you or didn't attract you to  modern warfare in the first place  modern warfare expanded call of duty  into more milsim territory with less  friendly weapons much larger maps  and larger modes that included vehicles  like ground war  if what attracted you to modern warfare  was that it was not like call of duty  then cold war might not live up to your  expectations  if you're looking for more traditional  call of duty with improvements then cold  war is probably going to be your thing  cold war and modern warfare share a lot  of the traditional modes  so let's talk about the unique ones cold  war has two in particular vip escort and  combined arms  full disclosure i'm more comfortable  talking about combined arms the combined  arms map shown so far are 12v12  that's against modern warfare's ground  war which has 32 32.  the water-based naval map in cold war  called armada is really unique and  very interesting but we're having a hard  time seeing combined arms being as good  as the larger ground war  could be wrong here player count alone  doesn't mean more fun it's about how a  map directs the number of players it has  but for now i'm going to give the larger  map modes to modern warfare  cold war also has vip escort which is a  unique mode that seems made for the cs  go crowd  modern warfare has a number of one life  modes that can probably go head to head  with this one  and i think we just need to see more of  this in cold war to make a determination  now one interesting mode that cold ward  has been teasing is called fire team  the first sub mode of which will be  called dirty bomb in that 10 teams of  four compete to gather resources  and arm bombs that detonate and cut off  sections of the map  this sounds pretty interesting it's like  a cross between modern warfare spec  ops and warzone as someone who's  completed every spec ops mission in  modern warfare  i can honestly say that it's admirable  but kind of half baked  and cold war's take sounds much better  for now we're gonna give this one at  least in concept to cold war  there's so much more we could talk about  and cold war has more reveals coming up  what are your biggest hopes and fears  for cold war right now are you ready to  leave modern warfare  behind let us know in the comments below  thanks for watching  you

